  "body": "## BLOCKED / needs_followup / DO NOT MERGE\n\nThis remains an honest noncanonical Bathcat evidence-gap packet, **not** a canonical-readiness claim or merge request. Keep it open, draft, and unmerged until the external evidence gaps close and a wholly fresh Mennonite audits the repaired exact head.\n\n- **Scout:** Bathcat \u2014 Field Intelligence and Knowledge Scout\n- **Target edition:** updated Unsettled framework printed for Orange Nebula's 2023 campaign, scoped to the retail framework bundle with Planets 001 Wenora and 002 Grakkis\n- **Audited head returned REVISE:** `030f0a8a343988996edfb69b62c682ed017c67eb`\n- **Intermediate repaired head:** `cac06848d8330a1faf71ab9ec3e252d708c5a629`\n- **Current corrected exact head:** `143ed8d473dc3adccbfe7f74fc60a1fa5d49cba5`\n- **Base:** `e0e47b2f7593f5ee34c25c5695be9b6bed172afd`\n- **No canonical staging tree:** intentional; blocked packets may not stage canonical content\n\n## Coverage\n\n### Governing rules\n\nDenominator: three complete governing authorities required to play the scoped bundle:\n\n1. updated framework rulebook;\n2. complete Planet 001 Wenora rules-bearing corpus;\n3. complete Planet 002 Grakkis rules-bearing corpus.\n\nAchieved: **1/3 = 33.3%** versus **100% required**. The acquired authority is the complete 48-page 2023-03-14 updated framework rulebook from a retailer mirror. The mirror is `provenance: secondary`; it is not a publisher-hosted rulebook receipt. Planet-specific special rules and survival-task materials remain missing.\n\n### Factual coverage\n\nDenominator: ten explicit claim groups recorded in `evidence.json`: edition identity, cooperative format, player count, modular framework/planet structure, three-die action economy, time/endurance pressure, exact updated framework component manifest, exact Planet 001 manifest, exact Planet 002 manifest, and official FAQ/errata applicability. Reviews, opinions, ratings, accessories, translations, additional planets, and unreleased products have zero weight.\n\nAchieved: **7/10 = 70.0%** versus **60% required**. Rulebook pages 4\u20135, **Component List / Base Framework**, close the exact updated framework component manifest under `src-002`. This corrected factual threshold does not overcome the failed governing-rules, official-provenance, and visual gates.\n\n## Retrieved evidence preserved\n\n- Orange Nebula campaign product page via Gamefound: https://gamefound.com/en/projects/orange-nebula/unsettled-/products/details/25486\n- Complete updated framework rulebook mirror: https://gamers-hq.de/media/pdf/g0/91/9d/Unsettled_Rulebook.pdf \u2014 69,217,668 bytes; SHA-256 `2cc105d5430e176b2bb45265809c5adf0ea7f7e3dcde1b3546a3f66ab4f47a59`; 48 pages; pages 4\u20135 contain the Base Framework component list\n- Independent review: https://thomaspking.com/2022/11/27/board-game-review-unsettled/\n- Independent review: https://www.stackup.org/post/ttrpg-review-unsettled\n- Meaningful review-linked gameplay visual: receipted as `src-005` in `evidence.json`\n\nThe two reviews, retailer-mirror provenance, and the single visual receipt remain unchanged.\n\n## Corrected official-source attempt ledger\n\nGamefound exposed the official locator `https://www.orangenebula.com/creations/unsettled/`. A bounded request redirected to `https://orangenebula.com/collections/unsettled` and returned HTTP 429; the official location is therefore recorded, but **no official rulebook file was retrieved**.\n\nExact sitemap receipts:\n\n| URL | Observed (UTC) | Result | Bytes | SHA-256 |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n| `https://orangenebula.com/sitemap.xml` | 2026-07-31T20:37:33Z | HTTP 200; `application/xml; charset=utf-8`; final URL unchanged | 6,769 | `1a585c058a0828816ab781dd2e798d5d1f6e537083801990a87479cf54f4c309` |\n| `https://orangenebula.com/sitemap_pages_1.xml?from=122794770715&to=181908570395` | 2026-07-31T20:37:33Z | HTTP 200; `application/xml; charset=utf-8`; final URL unchanged | 6,284 | `6d5a074cde9f4e696886f58b6e7ac64ec227e22f5d1c1eb8bedc1e745cc0af6c` |\n| `https://orangenebula.com/sitemap_products_1.xml?from=8248430199067&to=10353100325147` | 2026-07-31T20:37:33Z | HTTP 200; `application/xml; charset=utf-8`; final URL unchanged | 62,326 | `7ee0fdc8b854955a31e9f947720a16dd3f84d7d17ff6afbab927ab48a69a0bf2` |\n| `https://orangenebula.com/sitemap_collections_1.xml?from=436751630619&to=512344031515` | 2026-07-31T20:37:56Z | HTTP 200; `application/xml; charset=utf-8`; final URL unchanged | 6,596 | `dfe6050532b61ac18085b25711a54f3fb3b1e8271e18350fc25135a5f743a635` |\n\nThe English children enumerate two Unsettled page locators, 17 product locators, and two collection locators. One bounded request each inspected both pages, the two scope-relevant products (`framework-and-planets-001-2` and `survival-task-pack-1-2`), and both collections; each returned HTTP 429, `text/plain`, 18 bytes, SHA-256 `fa2dd01ed96d38758e89e354653c39f366bc7a34e485772c8aa2174b53a465d3`. The rate limits are preserved as observed failures, with **no publisher-absence inference**. The bare non-parameterized child URL's prior HTTP 400/zero-byte result is not treated as the result for the parameterized child sitemap.\n\nFull per-endpoint outcomes are recorded in `manifest.json`.\n\n## Residual external gaps\n\n- No publisher-hosted updated framework PDF has been receipted.\n- Complete Planet 001 Wenora and Planet 002 Grakkis rules-bearing materials, including planet-specific rules and survival tasks, remain unacquired.\n- Exact Planet 001 and Planet 002 component/rules manifests remain open. The updated framework manifest is no longer a residual gap.\n- Only one meaningful visual is receipted; promotion requires 4\u20138 distinct references plus a contact sheet.\n- Official FAQ/errata applicability to this printing remains unclosed.\n\n## Exact help requested from T\n\n1. Provide or authorize a publisher-hosted updated framework rulebook URL and the complete Planet 001 Wenora and Planet 002 Grakkis rules-bearing materials for this edition.\n2. Provide permission-cleared official component/gameplay images, or approve exact official asset URLs suitable for four distinct reduced editorial references.\n\n## Files and validation\n\nRepair commit changed only:\n\n- `TELEMETRY.md` \u2014 two deterministic final-writer rows\n- `intake/runs/2026-07-31-unsettled/manifest.json`\n- `intake/runs/2026-07-31-unsettled/candidates/unsettled/evidence.json`\n\nLocal gates on repaired head:\n\n- focused `node scripts/validate-intake.mjs --run 2026-07-31-unsettled` \u2014 clean\n- final writer sequence: `node scripts/generate-index.mjs`; `node scripts/validate-okf.mjs` \u2014 2,611 files clean; index fresh\n- complete local test denominator (intake/provenance/visual suites) \u2014 37 tests: 36 passed, 1 intentional skip, 0 failed\n- `node .claude/hooks/okf-guard.mjs self-test` \u2014 green\n- committed-head `node scripts/validate-intake.mjs --base e0e47b2f7593f5ee34c25c5695be9b6bed172afd` \u2014 clean\n- `git diff --check e0e47b2f7593f5ee34c25c5695be9b6bed172afd...143ed8d473dc3adccbfe7f74fc60a1fa5d49cba5` \u2014 clean\n- exact-head CI: [validate run 30664262026, job 91267415974](https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30664262026/job/91267415974) \u2014 **SUCCESS**, `headSha` `143ed8d473dc3adccbfe7f74fc60a1fa5d49cba5`\n\nBathcat did not approve, promote, mark ready, merge, create `approval.json`, or write under `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/games/`. Receiver order: **Judge, then a wholly fresh Mennonite audit bound only to current corrected head `143ed8d473dc3adccbfe7f74fc60a1fa5d49cba5`**.\n\n",
